# Stage 07 — Translate chapters (slim calls)

Translate every `chapters/src/{NNN_slug}.md` into `chapters/translated/{NNN_slug}.md`.

For each not-yet-translated chapter, in order:
1. Read the source chapter.
2. Build a SLIM translation context: the source passage (chapter or block group),
   the top 5-8 rules from `glossary/style_guide.md`, and ONLY the glossary terms
   actually hit in this chapter (grep `glossary/terms.csv` against the source).
   Do NOT load the whole glossary, full skills, or any EPUB/release rules.
3. Produce natural, faithful {{ target_lang }} prose. Output translation ONLY —
   no QA notes, no explanations, no source-term parentheses for ordinary nouns.
4. Write `chapters/translated/{NNN_slug}.md`.

Process chapters one at a time. Use `glob chapters/src/*.md` and
`glob chapters/translated/*.md` to track progress.

When all chapters in `chapters/src/` have a counterpart in `chapters/translated/`,
call `set_state` -> `TRANSLATED`, step `07_translate_chapters`.

Exit condition: every source chapter has a translated counterpart; state TRANSLATED.
